{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5194-1","published":"2026-11-11T12:32:44Z","modified":"2026-11-12T12:15:04.868768368Z","related":["CVE-2026-112390","CVE-2026-112391","CVE-2026-112392","CVE-2026-112393","CVE-2026-112394","CVE-2026-112395","CVE-2026-112397","CVE-2026-112398","CVE-2026-112399","CVE-2026-112400","CVE-2026-112401","CVE-2026-112402","CVE-2026-112403","CVE-2026-112404","CVE-2026-112405","CVE-2026-112406","CVE-2026-112891","CVE-2026-112892","CVE-2026-112894","CVE-2026-112895","CVE-2026-112896","CVE-2026-112897","CVE-2026-112898","CVE-2026-112899","CVE-2026-112900","CVE-2026-112901","CVE-2026-112902","CVE-2026-96636","CVE-2026-96637","CVE-2026-96638","CVE-2026-96640","CVE-2026-96641","CVE-2026-96642","CVE-2026-96778"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-112390","CVE-2026-112391","CVE-2026-112392","CVE-2026-112393","CVE-2026-112394","CVE-2026-112395","CVE-2026-112397","CVE-2026-112398","CVE-2026-112399","CVE-2026-112400","CVE-2026-112401","CVE-2026-112402","CVE-2026-112403","CVE-2026-112404","CVE-2026-112405","CVE-2026-112406","CVE-2026-112891","CVE-2026-112892","CVE-2026-112894","CVE-2026-112895","CVE-2026-112896","CVE-2026-112897","CVE-2026-112898","CVE-2026-112899","CVE-2026-112900","CVE-2026-112901","CVE-2026-112902","CVE-2026-96636","CVE-2026-96637","CVE-2026-96638","CVE-2026-96640","CVE-2026-96641","CVE-2026-96642","CVE-2026-96778"],"summary":"Security update for python-Pillow","details":"This update for python-Pillow fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-96636: decompression-bomb protection bypass via multi-frame `seek()` in MPO and DCX (bsc#1286802).\n- CVE-2026-96637: decompression bomb check bypass in `SpiderImagePlugin.seek()` leads to unbounded allocation DoS\n  (bsc#1286801).\n- CVE-2026-96638: BMP RLE decoder memory-amplification DoS via unbounded delta escape/absolute mode (bsc#1286800).\n- CVE-2026-96640: PDF append accepts malformed shared page-tree DAG, which can cause resource exhaustion (bsc#1286798).\n- CVE-2026-96641: reachable undefined behavior in native integer operations can lead to denial of service or logic\n  integrity compromise (bsc#1286797).\n- CVE-2026-96642: `TarIO` negative size field causes infinite CPU-spin loop (bsc#1286796).\n- CVE-2026-96778: heap buffer overflow writing JPEG comment after ICC profile fills buffer (bsc#1286793).\n- CVE-2026-112390: Denial of Service via infinite loop during crafted MIC image parsing (bsc#1286256).\n- CVE-2026-112391: Denial of Service via unbounded recursion in PDF parser (bsc#1286273).\n- CVE-2026-112392: Denial of Service via zero-size images in rank filters (bsc#1286287).\n- CVE-2026-112393: heap buffer overflow and stale-heap disclosure in _tiffWriteProc when saving compressed TIFF data\n  (bsc#1286325).\n- CVE-2026-112394: `P;2L` and `P;4L` decoders may read 1 to 3 bytes past the passed buffer size (bsc#1286311).\n- CVE-2026-112395: Pillow tiled-TIFF decoder reads past tile buffer in `copy4` (bsc#1286312).\n- CVE-2026-112397: out-of-bounds access in `_imagingmorph` on a zero-width image (bsc#1286314).\n- CVE-2026-112398: heap buffer overflow in FPX JPEG decoding can lead to code execution (bsc#1286406).\n- CVE-2026-112399: Denial of service via crafted APNG image (bsc#1286368).\n- CVE-2026-112400: Denial of Service via memory exhaustion from crafted GIF image (bsc#1286370).\n- CVE-2026-112401: Denial of Service via crafted GIF comments (bsc#1286372).\n- CVE-2026-112402: Denial of service via double free during image transformation (bsc#1286381).\n- CVE-2026-112403: heap buffer overflow in `ImagingJpegDecode` allows for code execution (bsc#1286405).\n- CVE-2026-112404: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds read in TIFF decoding (bsc#1286388).\n- CVE-2026-112405: NULL pointer dereference in `Image.merge` via an unvalidated band 0 (bsc#1286404).\n- CVE-2026-112406: infinite loop in `PdfParser.rewrite_pages` on page tree `Parent` cycle (bsc#1286403).\n- CVE-2026-112891: quadratic GIF comment copying during save (bsc#1286402).\n- CVE-2026-112892: MSP RLE decoder expands a tiny file into unbounded memory (bsc#1286401).\n- CVE-2026-112894: Denial of Service via crafted multi-frame image conversion (bsc#1286408).\n- CVE-2026-112895: Denial of service via crafted PDF during append operations (bsc#1286411).\n- CVE-2026-112896: TIFF encoder `ColorMap` plane-size mismatch causes a heap out-of-bounds read (bsc#1286400).\n- CVE-2026-112897: `TiffDecode` returns uninitialized memory as pixels for short JPEG strips (bsc#1286398).\n- CVE-2026-112898: `Image.quantize()` with empty palette can leak uninitialized stack memory (bsc#1286399).\n- CVE-2026-112899: EPS `load(scale)` lets Ghostscript render past the decompression bomb limit (bsc#1286489).\n- CVE-2026-112900: argument Injection in Ghostscript call can lead to remote code execution (bsc#1286397).\n- CVE-2026-112901: ReDoS in `XbmImagePlugin` can be triggered by 512-byte file (bsc#1286396).\n- CVE-2026-112902: memory disclosure and segfault in libtiff encoder via crafted TIFF tags (bsc#1286804).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python-Pillow","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Module for Python 3 15 SP7","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python-Pillow&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Module%20for%20Python%203%2015%20SP7"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.5.0-150400.5.28.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"python311-Pillow":"9.5.0-150400.5.28.1","python311-Pillow-tk":"9.5.0-150400.5.28.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5194-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"python-Pillow","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-ESPOS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python-Pillow&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-ESPOS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.5.0-150400.5.28.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"python311-Pillow":"9.5.0-150400.5.28.1","python311-Pillow-tk":"9.5.0-150400.5.28.